NVIDIA CUDA 12.6 redistributable components (CUDA plugin artifacts only)
  The Linux CUDA plugins statically incorporate libcudadevrt and
  libcudart_static. Their compilation can also incorporate libdevice.10.bc
  and CUB headers from CCCL 2.5.0. They do not link or redistribute cuRAND.

  libcudadevrt, libcudart_static, and libdevice are NVIDIA Redistributable
  Software under the CUDA Toolkit 12.6 EULA and its Attachment A. CUB is
  covered by the CCCL 2.5.0 license. CUDA release bundles carry the exact
  applicable license materials as:
    NVIDIA-CUDA-12.6-EULA.pdf
    NVIDIA-CCCL-2.5.0-LICENSE
  The bundled EULA bytes are the official CUDA 12.6 PDF (also applicable to
  the 12.6 Update 3 toolkit used for these plugins). Versioned references:
    https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/12.6.0/pdf/EULA.pdf
    https://github.com/NVIDIA/cccl/blob/v2.5.0/LICENSE

  These proprietary/BSD-licensed NVIDIA inputs are not GNU GPL Corresponding
  Source. The separate corresponding-source asset closes the GNU/MinGW source
  mappings without representing NVIDIA toolkit archives as GPL source.
